-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5314+) **Found-value** evaluation now uses **`int`** end-to-end (CitySiteEvaluator, AIFoundValue, CvPlot cache, SPI, Python callback), **not `short`**. Why: **avoid overflow/underflow** and short wraparounds in site scoring; keep the logic the same while **improving reliability**. Expectation: more robust site values, fewer edge-case penalties/boosts from short overflow; no known negative gameplay change. Performance: `int` is typically at least as fast as short on modern CPUs; no slowdown expected. Tested: autoplay ran fine. See [Change from short to int the Found value pipeline](/README.md#change-from-short-to-int-the-found-value-pipeline).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5335+) Removed the old clunky Base AdvCiv's `CONCEPT_TRAIT` XML clutter. Now using the more efficient `WIDGET_PYTHON` similarly instead.
